course: dictionary
lesson: 6763
title: Operate: work, run and control
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Operate is a doing word, a verb. Its main meaning is to make something work or to control it. «The buses operate every ten minutes» tells you the buses run every ten minutes.
explain: Context helps you choose the right meaning. «A surgeon is a doctor who operates on the body.» The words doctor and body show that operate here means a doctor cuts into a patient to fix something.
explain: To check a meaning, swap it into the sentence. Try work or run in the bus sentence, and it still makes sense. Try it in the surgeon sentence and you will see that a different meaning is needed.
fact: Operate is a verb. Its other forms are operates, operated and operating.
fact: «Operate» means to make a machine work or to control it.
fact: «Operate» can also mean to work or run, as in «The buses operate every ten minutes.»
fact: A surgeon is a doctor who operates on the body to fix something.
fact: In maths, operations are adding, subtracting, multiplying and dividing, and you operate on numbers.
exercise: «A surgeon is a doctor who operates on the body.» What does operates mean here? | Sleeps in the hospital | *Cuts into a patient to fix something | Sings loudly to the patient | Writes down what is wrong
exercise: «The buses operate every ten minutes.» What does operate mean? | Paint and decorate | Stop and wait | *Run or work | Argue about the time
exercise: In maths, what do you operate on? | Pictures | *Numbers | Doors | Words
test: In safety lessons, who should operate dangerous machines? | Pets | Children who are fast | *Only adults | Anyone who is bored
test: Which word fits? The pilot will ___ the plane. | Sleep | Ignore | *Operate | Forget
exam: Which word best fits? The charity ___ food banks across the city. | glows | sleeps | *operates | whispers
